  help: repo.kdl holds `schema-version`, `buildc-version`, `name`, `base-url`,
        `registry`, `backend`, `seed`, a `builds` block, a `github` block, a
        `libraries` block, a `library` block, a `renovate` block, a `manifest`
        block, an `audit` block and a `security-policy` block. These nodes
        state what is true of the repository. An image is the component that a
        build in `builds` names

